Subject: local: run the triage sandbox on a CA-bearing image

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. Breadboard-local substitution, recorded under decision 3 of
the Fullsend integration conformance plan.

The sandbox supervisor builds its upstream TLS trust from the system bundle
when it starts. The conformance forge is served by a cert-manager CA that
exists only in this cluster, so without that CA present before the supervisor
starts, every proxied HTTPS request to the forge fails its handshake and the
agent sees a connection reset. Uploading a CA afterwards does not help: the
roots are read once.

The OpenShell chart at the deployed version exposes no way to inject a CA into
sandbox pods, so the CA has to be in the image.

fullsend-sandbox-local:k3s is built FROM the exact digest this file pinned,
adding only ca-certificates and the cluster CA. It is that image plus one
recorded layer, not a substitute assembled elsewhere. See
deploy/fullsend-sandbox-local/Containerfile and the build step in
deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh, which fails rather than shipping an image
whose trust store is wrong.

Drop this patch if the chart gains sandbox CA injection, or if the forge is
ever served by a publicly trusted certificate.

Breadboard note: applied to the agents mirror by
deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-upstream-agents.py.

diff --git a/harness/triage.yaml b/harness/triage.yaml
index 889e41c..b2bf3d0 100644
--- a/harness/triage.yaml
+++ b/harness/triage.yaml
@@ -9,7 +9,13 @@ model: opus
 # effort is unset (internal/runtime/pi_run.go piDefaultThinking). Revisit
 # when the model: above moves to a generation with a different default.
 effort: high
-image: ghcr.io/fullsend-ai/fullsend-sandbox@sha256:259605fea321353552fdefd3a6a55e8b5c260998dfc5a622ed143e41a429995a
+# Breadboard-local: the image above, plus this cluster's internal CA. The
+# sandbox supervisor reads its upstream TLS roots from the system bundle
+# once at startup, and the conformance forge is served by a CA that exists
+# only here, so without it every proxied HTTPS request to the forge fails
+# its handshake. Built by deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh FROM the
+# digest above, so this is that image plus one layer.
+image: fullsend-sandbox-local:k3s
 policy: policies/base.yaml
 openshell:
   profiles:
